  "notes": "{注|さ}す means to pour or apply liquid in small amounts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\nSeveral verbs are read さす but use different kanji:\n- {注|さ}す: to pour, apply (liquid)\n- {刺|さ}す: to stab, pierce\n- {指|さ}す: to point at\n- {挿|さ}す: to insert\n- {差|さ}す: to hold up (umbrella), to shine (light)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {目薬|めぐすり}を{注|さ}す: to put in eye drops\n- {油|あぶら}を{注|さ}す: to oil, lubricate\n- お{酒|さけ}を{注|さ}す: to pour sake (for someone)\n- {水|みず}を{注|さ}す: to add water, to throw cold water on (figuratively)\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nIn the context of serving drinks, especially sake, {注|さ}す implies pouring for someone else as a gesture of hospitality.",
